            <ArticleTitle>Coronary bypass surgery in patients with Sheehan's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1264-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a small series of patients with Sheehan's syndrome (postpartum panhypopituitarism) and coronary artery disease. All four had uneventful coronary bypass grafting. We have successfully managed these patients peri-operatively by using intravenous hydrocortisone and oral thyroxin replacement.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
